[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4340590624","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119055#issuecomment-4340590624","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119055","id":4340590624,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABArgoIA","user":{"login":"theXYZT","id":172810,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MjgxMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/172810?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT","html_url":"https://github.com/theXYZT","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-29T03:20:18Z","updated_at":"2026-04-29T03:20:18Z","body":"You don't use `class_name` with autoloads as they are named in the project settings.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4340590624/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4341334251","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119055#issuecomment-4341334251","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119055","id":4341334251,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAsOA6w","user":{"login":"vadimmos","id":14206443,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MjA2NDQz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14206443?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vadimmos","html_url":"https://github.com/vadimmos","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vadimmos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vadimmos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vadimmos/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vadimmos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vadimmos/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vadimmos/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vadimmos/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vadimmos/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vadimmos/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-29T06:09:54Z","updated_at":"2026-04-29T06:09:54Z","body":"The name of a class that is used in other scripts for type checking is one thing, but the name of a global variable that stores a reference to an object is another matter. Both are located in the global namespace, which is why they conflict. the problem is that I can't add a global node and I've replaced it because it's not added with the default name. Why not display, for example, a rename dialog in case of a conflict?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4341334251/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4341617787","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119055#issuecomment-4341617787","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119055","id":4341617787,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAsfUew","user":{"login":"theXYZT","id":172810,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MjgxMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/172810?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT","html_url":"https://github.com/theXYZT","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-29T07:13:53Z","updated_at":"2026-04-29T07:16:04Z","body":"<img width=\"625\" height=\"94\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/23c30eba-9500-482c-b117-d4bad6fd5b3d\" />\n\nThe warning message is literally displayed as you are typing in the textbox. You can literally choose to rename the node in that exact moment -- just keep typing.\n\nIf you are adding a script with a `class_name` defined. Then, simply don't do that.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4341617787/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":2,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4343145306","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119055#issuecomment-4343145306","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119055","id":4343145306,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAt8jWg","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-29T11:10:50Z","updated_at":"2026-04-29T11:10:50Z","body":"> You don't use `class_name` with autoloads as they are named in the project settings.\n\n> If you are adding a script with a `class_name` defined. Then, simply don't do that.\n\nIt's perfectly fine to use `class_name` in an autoloaded script exposed as some global name as long as such names are unique.\nYou can be recommending to not use it like that for whatever reason but technically there's nothing wrong about it.\n\n> <img alt=\"Image\" width=\"625\" height=\"94\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/172810/585251897-23c30eba-9500-482c-b117-d4bad6fd5b3d.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJnaXRodWIuY29tIiwiYXVkIjoicmF3LmdpdGh1YnVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbSIsImtleSI6ImtleTUiLCJleHAiOjE3Nzc0NTk4MjQsIm5iZiI6MTc3NzQ1OTUyNCwicGF0aCI6Ii8xNzI4MTAvNTg1MjUxODk3LTIzYzMwZWJhLTk1MDAtNDgyYy1iMTE3LWQ0YmFkNmZkNWIzZC5wbmc_.ETpj07xpz_a4sjmGtfzhaydOh-W0QVTvXmykCXLu7hg\">\n> \n> The warning message is literally displayed as you are typing in the textbox. You can literally choose to rename the node in that exact moment -- just keep typing.\n\nJudging by the screenshot it seems you're testing this in an older version where the issue is not present. The report refers to v4.7.beta1.official [1c8cc9e7e].\n\n- v4.6.2.stable.official [71f334935], you can add a `class_name`d script as an autoload as long as you change the name:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4c7bbfc3-1c0d-416e-8f44-8fcaf149ffa0\n\n- v4.7.beta1.official [1c8cc9e7e], no way to change the name before the addition, and hence can't add such autoload in case the script's used `class_name` conflicts with the script name after capitalization etc. (which is used as the default name for the autoload being added):\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/90b59d7c-02c7-4105-a802-3cf0c1868818\n\nAs a workaround in v4.7.beta1.official [1c8cc9e7e] you could e.g.:\n1. Temporarily remove `class_name` from the script to be added as an autoload.\n2. Add such script as autoload.\n3. Change the added autoload name to something different.\n4. Readd the previous `class_name` in the script.\n\nAnd it will work just fine, as in the previous versions.\n\nAll in all, this is a regression in functionality for this specific use case (wouldn't call it a bug, rather an unintentionally (?) removed functionality).\nThe regression is a result of #91124. cc @KoBeWi ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4343145306/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4343707012","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119055#issuecomment-4343707012","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119055","id":4343707012,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAue1hA","user":{"login":"theXYZT","id":172810,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MjgxMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/172810?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT","html_url":"https://github.com/theXYZT","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-29T12:37:03Z","updated_at":"2026-04-29T12:37:17Z","body":"Thanks for pointing this out, @kleonc -- how embarrassing for me! While we're at it, it might be nice to:\n\n1. Add tooltips to the buttons explaining what they do.\n2. [Fix the docs which still show the old UI on \"latest\".](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/tutorials/scripting/singletons_autoload.html#doc-singletons-autoload)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4343707012/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4344364051","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119055#issuecomment-4344364051","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119055","id":4344364051,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAvG8Ew","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubuserc